        "code": {
          "text": "Visual acuity"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 6/9 in each eye on Snellen testing in the room; testing was repeated because the patient was distractible. Able to read a number plate across the car park."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left eye symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent redness and mild irritation, especially after full days working in wind and dust; occasional gritty sensation relieved by blinking or rinsing; mild end-of-day dryness; end-of-day blur settles after overnight rest. Driving, including at night, and reading are reported as okay."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Eye symptoms denied"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies significant pain, photophobia, discharge, foreign-body sensation, trauma, halos, diplopia, and headache."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Left eye examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Nasal conjunctival fibrovascular triangular growth extending approximately 2.5–3 mm onto the cornea from the limbus, not near the visual axis; mild conjunctival injection around the lesion. No ulceration, obvious dellen, or purulent discharge."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right eye examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Small nasal pinguecula or very early pterygium-like change, with no corneal involvement; asymptomatic."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Pupils and eye movements"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Pupils equal and round, reactive to light; no relative afferent pupillary defect. Extraocular movements full; no diplopia. Lids within normal limits."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Fluorescein examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Basic fluorescein check showed no abrasion or ulcer; tear film slightly irregular over the pterygium only."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
